# Docker build context for the Dockerfile at the repo root. ALLOW-LIST: everything is excluded, then only the
# files the image needs are let back in. This keeps secrets (.env), downloaded data (data/), local caches
# (.venv, node_modules, .cache, qdrant_storage), results/ and the git history out of the build context.

# 1. Exclude everything.
*

# 2. Let back in what the Dockerfile copies.
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!src/
!config/
!corpus/
!frontend/

# 3. Inside those folders, exclude build output, dependencies, caches and anything secret-looking.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.DS_Store
frontend/node_modules
frontend/.next
frontend/out
frontend/*.tsbuildinfo
frontend/next-env.d.ts
frontend/npm-debug.log*
# Frontend dev helpers that are not part of the build (screenshots need Python + Playwright).
frontend/scripts/screenshots.py
